Chapter: BrowserNewtabOverflowTest
  cites Browser chapter Browser
  cites Browser chapter BrowserTheme
  cites Browser chapter Display
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 WORKS-41 asks where the newtab page's content goes when the box it is given
 is shorter than the content. The question is decidable without a screen, a
 face or a pointer: it is `widget-layout` over the tree `browser-render`
 builds.

 IT DRIVES THE FUNCTIONS `gbr-repaint` ITSELF DRIVES -- `browser-init`,
 `browser-scroll-fit`, `browser-render`, `widget-layout` and
 `browser-laid-viewport`, in that order and with the same arguments. A row
 that re-derived the page's rects beside them would be a SHADOW of the
 painter's arithmetic, free to drift from it while both stayed green.

 THE WIDTH IS HELD AT 1024 AND ONLY THE HEIGHT MOVES, so any difference
 between the rows is the height's doing and not a reflow's. The three heights
 are chosen so the two candidate answers disagree: 768 is the mode the
 backlog row reports, 400 is shorter than the content by more than one row,
 and 1600 is taller than the content. **The 1600 row is the control.** A
 layout that pushed every child past its box, or a probe that counted nodes
 it should not, would report a non-zero count there too.

 The rows print the PAYLOAD -- each child's top, height and bottom against
 the box -- rather than a verdict computed from it. A row printing only "the
 page overflows" would agree with an implementation that put every child at
 the same coordinate.

Section: Body

  bn-yn : Boolean -> Text
  bn-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  bn-top : WidgetNode -> Integer
  bn-top (n) = let b = n.wn-bounds in b.lr-y

  bn-h : WidgetNode -> Integer
  bn-h (n) = let b = n.wn-bounds in b.lr-h

  bn-bot : WidgetNode -> Integer
  bn-bot (n) = let b = n.wn-bounds in b.lr-y + b.lr-h

  bn-laid : Integer, Integer -> WidgetNode
  bn-laid (w) (h) =
    let st = browser-init w h browser-theme-default display-init-text-fallback
    in let fit = browser-scroll-fit st w h
    in widget-layout (browser-render fit) (fit.bs-theme) (layout-rect 0 0 w h)

 THE COUNT IS THE ASSERTION AND THE TABLE IS NOT. It walks the whole page
 subtree rather than the direct children, because a link button sits one
 level down inside the `links` panel and it is the link rows the report is
 about.

  bn-past-kids : List WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  bn-past-kids (ks) (n) (i) (limit) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else let one = bn-past (list-at ks i) limit
    in bn-past-kids ks n (i + 1) limit (acc + one)

  bn-past : WidgetNode, Integer -> Integer
  bn-past (n) (limit) =
    let self = if bn-bot n > limit then 1 else 0
    in let kids = bn-past-kids (n.wn-children) (n.wn-child-count) 0 limit 0
    in self + kids

  bn-child-row : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Text
  bn-child-row (vp) (i) (limit) =
    let c = list-at (vp.wn-children) i
    in "  " & c.wn-id
       & " y " & integer-to-text (bn-top c)
       & " h " & integer-to-text (bn-h c)
       & " bottom " & integer-to-text (bn-bot c)
       & "  past " & bn-yn (bn-bot c > limit)

  bn-print-kids : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bn-print-kids (vp) (i) (n) (limit) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else act
      print-line-uni (bn-child-row vp i limit)
      bn-print-kids vp (i + 1) n limit
    end

  bn-head : Integer, Integer, WidgetNode -> Text
  bn-head (w) (h) (vp) =
    "box " & integer-to-text w & "x" & integer-to-text h
      & "  page root " & vp.wn-id
      & " y " & integer-to-text (bn-top vp)
      & " h " & integer-to-text (bn-h vp)
      & " bottom " & integer-to-text (bn-bot vp)
      & "  root past box " & bn-yn (bn-bot vp > h)

  bn-report : Integer, Integer, WidgetNode -> [Console] Nothing
  bn-report (w) (h) (vp) =
    let head = bn-head w h vp
    in let tail = "  nodes past the box bottom: " & integer-to-text (bn-past vp h)
    in act
      print-line-uni head
      p <- bn-print-kids vp 0 (vp.wn-child-count) h
      print-line-uni tail
    end

  bn-case : Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  bn-case (w) (h) =
    let laid = bn-laid w h
    in when browser-laid-viewport laid
      is None ->
        let miss = "box " & integer-to-text w & "x" & integer-to-text h & ": NO VIEWPORT -- the arm did not run"
        in act
          print-line-uni miss
        end
      is Just (vp) -> bn-report w h vp

Section: Opening

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    bn-case 1024 768
    bn-case 1024 400
    bn-case 1024 1600
    print-line-uni "the 1600 row is the control and must report zero"
  end
